6. Non-Functional Requirements
ID	Area	Requirement
NFR-01	Performance	Largest Contentful Paint under 2.5 s, Interaction to Next Paint under 200 ms, and Cumulative Layout Shift under 0.1, measured on a throttled mobile profile.
NFR-02	Performance	The homepage becomes interactive without waiting on carousel or video assets; offscreen media is deferred.
NFR-03	Accessibility	Conformance with WCAG 2.2 Level AA. No critical or serious violations from an automated scan, plus a manual keyboard and screen-reader pass.
NFR-04	Accessibility	Visible focus indicator on every interactive element; no keyboard trap in menus, carousels, or accordions.
NFR-05	Accessibility	Text contrast at least 4.5:1, and large text and interface components at least 3:1.
NFR-06	Responsive	Correct rendering at 360, 768, 1024, 1440, and 1920 pixels wide, with no horizontal scrolling and no overlapping content.
NFR-07	Compatibility	Current and previous major versions of Chrome, Firefox, Safari, and Edge, plus Safari on iOS and Chrome on Android.
NFR-08	SEO	A single H1, a unique title and meta description, a canonical tag, Open Graph and Twitter card metadata, and hreflang alternates for all six locales.
NFR-09	SEO	No broken internal links, no soft 404s, and a valid robots directive permitting indexing of the homepage.
NFR-10	Security	Site served over HTTPS with a valid certificate; HTTP requests redirect to HTTPS; security headers present.
NFR-11	Privacy	Consent mechanism appears where required by the visitor region, and analytics tags respect the recorded choice.
NFR-12	Reliability	No uncaught JavaScript errors in the console and no failed network requests on a clean page load.
NFR-13	Localisation	Each locale renders translated content with correct character encoding and no untranslated placeholder strings.
NFR-14	Analytics	The tag manager container loads and fires a page-view event; conversion controls emit their tracking events.
7. Test Approach
7.1 Method
- Manual exploratory and scripted execution for layout, content, and interaction.
- Automated link crawling for the link-integrity cases, limited to a depth of one from the homepage.
- Automated accessibility scanning with axe or an equivalent, followed by a manual keyboard pass, because automated tools catch roughly a third of real issues.
- Lighthouse and WebPageTest for the performance cases, run three times with the median taken.
- Browser developer tools for console errors, network failures, and response headers.
7.2 Test data
No credentials are used. Form validation cases use synthetic input only, and no form is ever submitted. Suggested invalid inputs: an empty string, a single space, an address missing the at sign, an address with a trailing dot, a 300-character string, a script tag, and a SQL fragment. These exercise client-side validation without creating records.
7.3 Entry and exit criteria
Gate	Criteria
Entry	The site is reachable, the test environment browsers are installed, and the baseline screenshots from the capture date are available.
Exit	All P0 cases executed with no open critical or high defects; at least 95% of P1 cases executed; all deviations documented.
7.4 Defect severity
Severity	Definition	Example
Critical	A conversion path or the navigation is unusable	Start for free leads to a 404
High	Major function broken with no workaround	A mega menu will not open on a supported browser
Medium	Function impaired but a workaround exists	Carousel arrows fail but swipe works
Low	Cosmetic or content issue	Inconsistent spacing in a footer column


