11. Assumptions and Risks
- The site is a live production property owned by a third party. Content and layout can change without notice, so any content-matching case should be re-baselined before a regression run.
- Marketing sites commonly run A/B tests. A tester may see a variant that differs from the captured baseline; treat a difference as a possible experiment before raising a defect.
- Geolocation affects the consent banner and some pricing content. Record the test location with each result.
- Link-integrity crawling should be rate-limited to avoid being treated as abusive traffic.
- Because no account exists, roughly the entire authenticated product surface is untested. If console coverage is later required, a separate specification and a test account will be needed.
